 very tight trade, lets see.","a":"FX.Sniffer","d":"","n":"#992","p":40,"im":["93672adbc01ecf1a83a0619d1406cebdd9245da9","49023140f054ead4c2447c2b33e173b8b672520e"],"m":992},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_993","t":"","a":"kruger","d":"","n":"#993","p":40,"im":["b6c2f71d0b355f3affff01c6785587ed23775425"],"m":993},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_994","t":"","a":"kruger","d":"","n":"#994","p":40,"im":["deece111f23e31440350db53bcab186aaaf3c780"],"m":994},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_995","t":"","a":"kruger","d":"","n":"#995","p":40,"im":["1d723358c97bceac6f7e08bf9a6c3c7216e570a4"],"m":995},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_996","t":"Just wanted to bring something to the attention of the people, which I caught by chance.\n\nThis is something which I spotted just now......take a look, so much of a coincidence!\n\nIn the hindsight, this is also a short trade which I am looking at on EurUsd.","a":"sunnytrader1984","d":"","n":"#996","p":40,"im":["3a9aab924f3073b2dcad85e67e21691b16f23be0"],"m":996},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_997","t":"If downward trendline holds potential long","a":"AlexC","d":"","n":"#997","p":40,"im":["b0425c7dd8852540ad2f4785bab6ffb54643b90a"],"m":997},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_998","t":"Haven't traded much today. Besides this EJ trade, I scalped the Aussie short and long.\n\n2nd Chart is larger","a":"danandsueco","d":"","n":"#998","p":40,"im":["598ce7c5d3b6ad035814a276043f932c487c5593","564ce7f87b0588322834f52a0e71570755f9840d"],"m":998},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_999","t":"I got this newsletter from Seiden showing some trades taken this week in his XLT course.\n\nlessons.tradingacademy.com/article/will-...rs-change-your-mind/\n\nthese are the images i managed to reconstruct on my platform.\n\ndo these trades make sense to the experts? what do you guys see in them?","a":"hornet","d":"","n":"#999","p":40,"im":["5f699d9cd066e2e4e05bd1ee049d39830720c1f2","3a8800b3267cafd308d50e83865e2babdf0e77a4"],"m":999},{"id":"supplydemand_p40_1000","t":"Hi Hornet. My 1st entry in the forum after saying hello!. I am a fan of Sam as I am sure we all are, but some trades invoke discussion, whether they are wrong, valid or right is debatable, whether I would have traded them is not, here my take: the 1st chart shows a very nice Supply zone, the speed of arrival to sams entry would have flagged a warning of a continuation, and I would want to see a confirmed slow down which we can all see after the event, the trade was valid the entry was naive.\n\nThe 2nd chart, shows a long period of trading where orders have been cleared, a weak release into a compressed short, not completing enough reward/distance before returning, this could easily be a fake and could have shot up as there was little resistance, not a trade for me.\n\nThe 3rd chart on M5 shows a group of trading more akin to compression following a previous supply/ignored/demand flip zone which would possibly have cleared many trades, it also does not fall away to any extent definitely not enough for a good R:R when all things are taken into account including spread etc, it has also been touched previousley and does not in any way fulfill the requirements.\n\nNo trades as shown for me! (1 trade at a later entry)\n\nWell just a nervous quick reply I hope it helps.just my take in a safe trading world Photize A short EDIT briefly looking again at the original charts on Sams website specifically the 2nd inspecting them, it looks more acceptable as it is on a different time-frame the ZONE look tighter and the Risk reward is improved. Different time-frames can offer different solutions please keep it in mind, evaluation must be made over a range of time frames for entries, My evaluation above is for the 3 graphs presented in the forum. cheers happy piping Photize","a":"photize","d":"","n":"#1000","p":40,"im":["a816e4392f7fde0fd70323ff62bde1fce69423a6"],"m":1000}],"images":[{"k":"65755a2ba1edca0d28c514d0c063cffbf2f3b31a","t":"assets/thumbs/65755a2ba1edca0d28c514d0c063cffbf2f3b31a.webp","f":"assets/images/65755a2ba1edca0d28c51